WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.112
(upbeat music)

00:00:01.112 --> 00:00:04.279
(audience applauding)

00:00:06.638 --> 00:00:07.471
- Hi guys!

00:00:08.840 --> 00:00:11.153
Oh, thanks for hanging out with us.

00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:16.540
Can I just share something
and be totally honest?

00:00:16.540 --> 00:00:18.530
I am rocking the caffeine this morning

00:00:18.530 --> 00:00:22.090
because I pulled an all-nighter
with my daughter, Frankie.

00:00:22.090 --> 00:00:23.350
Yep.

00:00:23.350 --> 00:00:25.700
I know, poor little sausage.

00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:27.430
She was in total discomfort

00:00:27.430 --> 00:00:29.980
and she couldn't go to the bathroom,

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:33.490
and Frankie, I so apologize
to your future self

00:00:33.490 --> 00:00:34.933
for telling this story,

00:00:36.770 --> 00:00:37.990
but I didn't know how to get around it.

00:00:37.990 --> 00:00:39.480
I was like, I should just tell the truth.

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:41.880
So basically around 9:00
PM, the pain started,

00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:45.700
and you cut to 9:30, 8:00
PM and we're in one bathroom

00:00:45.700 --> 00:00:47.770
and I'm like, "Frankie,
honey, it's going to be okay.

00:00:47.770 --> 00:00:50.420
Just don't push because
it's going to hurt more.

00:00:50.420 --> 00:00:53.960
You just got to relax your
body, and I have got you."

00:00:53.960 --> 00:00:56.990
Cut to 10:26, I administer Motrin.

00:00:56.990 --> 00:01:00.783
11:08, she accuses me of not
giving her real medicine.

00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:03.100
So I swear to her that the makers

00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:06.380
of Motrin have got her back.

00:01:06.380 --> 00:01:08.950
And at 1:02 AM, we're
now in the other bathroom

00:01:08.950 --> 00:01:11.700
and I'm hovering over her, still calm,

00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:13.890
once again telling her, "Don't push.

00:01:13.890 --> 00:01:15.860
It's going to be okay."

00:01:15.860 --> 00:01:18.330
And around 1:34, 43,

00:01:18.330 --> 00:01:20.517
I'm sitting on the bathroom
floor this time, like,

00:01:20.517 --> 00:01:22.010
"Don't push it.

00:01:22.010 --> 00:01:24.317
Just stop pushing."

00:01:25.450 --> 00:01:27.447
3:07 AM.

00:01:27.447 --> 00:01:29.240
"You want to watch "Hocus Pocus"?"

00:01:30.260 --> 00:01:32.660
And at 3:09, she says, "Mom, I'm cold."

00:01:32.660 --> 00:01:35.070
So I wrap her in a bunch
of blankets on the couch,

00:01:35.070 --> 00:01:36.967
and then at 3:17, she says,

00:01:36.967 --> 00:01:39.460
"Mom, I need more room on the couch."

00:01:39.460 --> 00:01:42.080
And I'm totally hanging off of it.

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:45.040
Okay, 3:28, "Mom, I'm still cold."

00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:47.810
And I give her my one
last blanket that's tiny

00:01:47.810 --> 00:01:50.597
and as I sit there freezing,
I look at her and I think,

00:01:50.597 --> 00:01:53.693
"I wouldn't have it any other way."

00:01:53.693 --> 00:01:55.525
(audience clapping)

00:01:55.525 --> 00:01:57.970
And the good news is it
turns out this morning,

00:01:57.970 --> 00:01:59.220
she's feeling great.

00:01:59.220 --> 00:02:00.530
Fresh as a daisy.

00:02:00.530 --> 00:02:04.270
Apparently no discomfort
whatsoever, so good news.

00:02:04.270 --> 00:02:06.750
Virtual friends, who was
in the all-nighters club

00:02:06.750 --> 00:02:08.650
with their kids?

00:02:08.650 --> 00:02:09.483
Katie and Lucy!

00:02:11.208 --> 00:02:12.343
Hi!
- Oh, yes.

00:02:12.343 --> 00:02:13.903
Actually, hi, Drew!

00:02:15.030 --> 00:02:16.670
- Oh, mothers and daughters, I love it.

00:02:16.670 --> 00:02:18.380
How are you guys?

00:02:18.380 --> 00:02:21.510
- Good, a big mommy hug to you.

00:02:21.510 --> 00:02:26.440
We all feel your pain, but we
know sickness or no sickness,

00:02:26.440 --> 00:02:28.900
being a mom, you never get any sleep,

00:02:28.900 --> 00:02:32.130
so we all feel your pain this morning.

00:02:32.130 --> 00:02:33.840
- Thank you so much,

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:37.030
and bless you to you and
your gorgeous daughter.

00:02:37.030 --> 00:02:39.720
And it's true, we'll do
anything for our kids.

00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:41.840
And sometimes we just
have to be honest about it

00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:42.890
instead of coming out here

00:02:42.890 --> 00:02:44.520
and pretending to be perfect all the time.

00:02:44.520 --> 00:02:45.690
I'm like, "I haven't slept.

00:02:45.690 --> 00:02:46.580
I feel nuts.

00:02:46.580 --> 00:02:47.430
Let's do this."

00:02:47.430 --> 00:02:50.970
You guys are rock stars, and
you do feel like a rock star

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:52.360
when you pull an all-nighter,

00:02:52.360 --> 00:02:55.550
just in a totally different way.

00:02:55.550 --> 00:02:57.030
And speaking of rock star moms,

00:02:57.030 --> 00:03:00.680
Gabrielle Union is on the show today.

00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:01.730
Oh, we love her!

00:03:01.730 --> 00:03:06.283
And now, let's kick it
off with some Drew's News.

00:03:07.151 --> 00:03:08.399
(brakes screeching)

00:03:08.399 --> 00:03:09.536
(cat meowing)

00:03:09.536 --> 00:03:11.870
(dramatic music)

00:03:11.870 --> 00:03:13.808
Excuse me, sir!

00:03:13.808 --> 00:03:14.641
Ma'am!

00:03:14.641 --> 00:03:15.910
Guy!

00:03:15.910 --> 00:03:17.173
Tell me your story!

00:03:19.420 --> 00:03:22.203
Ma'am, I asked you a question.

00:03:23.050 --> 00:03:24.717
This is Drew's News!

00:03:27.176 --> 00:03:28.440
This is Drew's News.

00:03:29.360 --> 00:03:30.463
It's Drew's News!

00:03:31.720 --> 00:03:34.370
(audience cheering)

00:03:34.370 --> 00:03:37.840
Every day, our team, we
come up with headlines

00:03:37.840 --> 00:03:40.660
to find stories that simply made us happy,

00:03:40.660 --> 00:03:43.213
and let's see what made the papers.

00:03:44.340 --> 00:03:46.570
Okay, you know sometimes
you just read a story

00:03:46.570 --> 00:03:50.100
and you're like, "Yes, I love humanity."

00:03:50.100 --> 00:03:52.250
And this one did that for me.

00:03:52.250 --> 00:03:54.320
It also made me hungry.

00:03:54.320 --> 00:03:58.610
Okay, I saw this morning,
Travel + Leisure reports

00:03:58.610 --> 00:04:00.030
that there's a new record

00:04:00.030 --> 00:04:03.020
for world's largest chocolate fountain.

00:04:03.020 --> 00:04:07.030
It's a 30-foot cascade of
melted chocolate falling

00:04:07.030 --> 00:04:10.080
into a big old Lindor.

00:04:10.080 --> 00:04:12.340
Oh yes, give it to me.

00:04:12.340 --> 00:04:15.640
I love sweet, but I'm also
maybe thinking nacho cheese

00:04:15.640 --> 00:04:17.280
might be better too?

00:04:17.280 --> 00:04:18.280
I don't know.

00:04:18.280 --> 00:04:21.180
Hey, virtual friends, sweet or savory?

00:04:21.180 --> 00:04:25.640
Samantha, which one floats your boat?

00:04:25.640 --> 00:04:27.180
- Me and the girls here, we choose.

00:04:27.180 --> 00:04:29.553
- [Girls] Both,
chocolate-covered pretzels.

00:04:31.350 --> 00:04:34.510
- I think pretzels and
chocolate and nacho cheese.

00:04:34.510 --> 00:04:39.100
I would get a little
Tostitos Scoop and rock it.

00:04:39.100 --> 00:04:39.990
Thanks, Samantha.

00:04:39.990 --> 00:04:42.630
Okay, well, good work Lindt.

00:04:42.630 --> 00:04:43.950
You made the world happy.

00:04:43.950 --> 00:04:46.580
And if chocolate fountains
aren't your thing,

00:04:46.580 --> 00:04:49.340
can I interest you in a wine backpack?

00:04:49.340 --> 00:04:50.540
You heard me.

00:04:50.540 --> 00:04:55.440
Fox News reports that
box wine maker Franzia

00:04:55.440 --> 00:04:58.790
has just developed a backpack that doubles

00:04:58.790 --> 00:05:00.920
as a wine dispenser.

00:05:00.920 --> 00:05:01.753
Uh huh.

00:05:01.753 --> 00:05:04.847
A crucial accessory for
any Merlot lover on the go.

00:05:04.847 --> 00:05:05.680
#merlotonthego.

00:05:07.680 --> 00:05:11.890
Franzia also announced
swimsuits, boxer shorts, socks,

00:05:11.890 --> 00:05:13.120
and other accessories.

00:05:13.120 --> 00:05:17.560
I mean, you guys, can you
imagine an entire outfit made out

00:05:17.560 --> 00:05:18.940
of Franzia products?

00:05:18.940 --> 00:05:22.317
It's like, "Who are you wearing?"

00:05:22.317 --> 00:05:24.637
"It's Franzia by Franzia."

00:05:26.470 --> 00:05:29.270
I feel like if you're rocking the Franzia

00:05:29.270 --> 00:05:31.270
and draining that backpack,
they're going to have to come up

00:05:31.270 --> 00:05:34.490
with a few more products
like Franzia electrolytes,

00:05:34.490 --> 00:05:37.430
Franzia mattresses for the old pass out,

00:05:37.430 --> 00:05:41.558
and maybe some morning
huevos rancheros by Franzia.

00:05:41.558 --> 00:05:44.920
(audience applauding)

00:05:44.920 --> 00:05:48.820
Okay, so moving on, this
next story really got me.

00:05:48.820 --> 00:05:52.280
According to a new study
reported by People Magazine,

00:05:52.280 --> 00:05:57.280
who we love, a dog's
heart rate increases 46%

00:05:57.410 --> 00:06:00.683
whenever its owner says I love you.

00:06:01.670 --> 00:06:04.150
I mean, can you even handle the sweetness?

00:06:04.150 --> 00:06:05.340
It's like, I can't.

00:06:05.340 --> 00:06:08.840
It's me and my girls, we have
two dogs, Douglas and Lucy.

00:06:08.840 --> 00:06:10.090
That's them.

00:06:10.090 --> 00:06:12.650
And it just makes me so happy to think

00:06:12.650 --> 00:06:15.030
that it gets our dog's heart racing

00:06:15.030 --> 00:06:17.513
when we say those three little words.

00:06:18.590 --> 00:06:22.100
And Douglas and Lucy, if
you're watching, I love you.

00:06:22.100 --> 00:06:23.273
I love you!

00:06:24.450 --> 00:06:28.160
So take some time to tell
your good boy or good girl

00:06:28.160 --> 00:06:29.463
that you love them too.

00:06:31.049 --> 00:06:33.632
(upbeat music)

